.TH "tclinterp::interpolation" 3tcl 0\&.15 "tclinterp" "Tcl wrapper for C interpolation procedures"
.SH NAME
tclinterp::interpolation - Commands in namespace tclinterp::interpolation
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcubicSpline1d\fP \fI-t values -y values -ti values ?-ibcbeg condition? ?-ibcend condition? ?-ybcbeg value? ?-ybcend value? ?-deriv? ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
\fBdivDif1d\fP \fI-x values -y values -xi values ?-coeffs? ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
\fBhermiteSpline1d\fP \fI-t values -y values -yp values -ti values ?-deriv? ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
\fBlagr1d\fP \fI-x values -y values -xi values ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
\fBleast1d\fP \fI-x values -y values -xi values ?-w values? ?-nterms integer? ?-coeffs? ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
\fBleast1dDer\fP \fI-x values -y values -xi values ?-w values? ?-nterms integer? ?-coeffs? ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
\fBlin1d\fP \fI-x values -y values -xi values ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
\fBnear1d\fP \fI-x values -y values -xi values ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
\fBpchip1d\fP \fI-x values -f values -xe values ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
.SH ::TCLINTERP::INTERPOLATION
.SH COMMANDS
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBcubicSpline1d\fR (::tclinterp::interpolation)
.RE
.PP
Performs piecewise cubic spline interpolation\&.
.RS 4n
\fBcubicSpline1d\fP \fI-t values -y values -ti values ?-ibcbeg condition? ?-ibcend condition? ?-ybcbeg value? ?-ybcend value? ?-deriv? ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-deriv
Include first and second derivatives in the result dictionary\&.
.TP
-ibcbeg condition
Left boundary condition: quad, der1, der2, or notaknot; defaults to quad\&. Alias: -begflag\&.
.TP
-ibcend condition
Right boundary condition: quad, der1, der2, or notaknot; defaults to quad\&. Alias: -endflag\&.
.TP
-ifexists error|replace
Policy for existing destination vectors; defaults to error\&. With replace, an existing real vector is resized and overwritten\&.
.TP
-input list|vector
Input representation for all array arguments: Tcl lists or real RBC vector names\&. Defaults to list\&.
.TP
-name name
Destination vector name for yi; requires -output vector\&. Omit it or use #auto to create an automatically named vector\&.
.TP
-names dictionary
Dictionary mapping output fields to destination vector names; requires -output vector\&. Valid fields: yi and, only with -deriv, yder1, yder2\&.
.TP
-output list|vector
Output representation for every numeric result array: Tcl list or RBC vector name\&. Defaults to list; independent of -input\&.
.TP
-t values
Strictly increasing sample positions; at least two values\&. Alias: -x\&.
.TP
-ti values
Evaluation positions; must not be empty\&. Alias: -xi\&.
.TP
-y values
Sample values; must have the same length as -t\&.
.TP
-ybcbeg value
Prescribed left endpoint derivative for der1 or der2; defaults to 0\&.0\&.
.TP
-ybcend value
Prescribed right endpoint derivative for der1 or der2; defaults to 0\&.0\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Every array argument marked values uses the representation selected by -input\&. Scalar options remain
ordinary Tcl numbers\&. Numeric inputs must be finite\&. RBC support must be enabled in the build to use
vectors\&.
.PP
Vector names resolve in the caller's namespace; destination namespaces must already exist\&. Each unnamed
output, including fields omitted from -names, is created with ::rbc::vector create #auto\&. Returned
vector names are fully qualified\&.
.PP
Do not specify both -name and the yi entry of -names\&. Unknown output fields and duplicate destinations
are errors\&. The caller owns returned vectors and can release them with ::rbc::vector destroy
$vectorName\&.
.PP
The boundary condition quad makes the first or last interval quadratic\&. The conditions der1 and der2
prescribe the first or second endpoint derivative using -ybcbeg or -ybcend, respectively for the left or
right endpoint\&. The condition notaknot makes the third derivative continuous at the first or last
interior knot and requires at least four samples\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
The interpolated values yi\&. With -deriv, returns a dictionary with yi, first derivatives
yder1, and second derivatives yder2\&. Each numeric array is a Tcl list by default or an RBC vector name
with -output vector\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBdivDif1d\fR (::tclinterp::interpolation)
.RE
.PP
Performs divided-difference polynomial interpolation\&.
.RS 4n
\fBdivDif1d\fP \fI-x values -y values -xi values ?-coeffs? ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-coeffs
Include the divided-difference coefficient array in the result dictionary\&.
.TP
-ifexists error|replace
Policy for existing destination vectors; defaults to error\&. With replace, an existing real vector is resized and overwritten\&.
.TP
-input list|vector
Input representation for all array arguments: Tcl lists or real RBC vector names\&. Defaults to list\&.
.TP
-name name
Destination vector name for yi; requires -output vector\&. Omit it or use #auto to create an automatically named vector\&.
.TP
-names dictionary
Dictionary mapping output fields to destination vector names; requires -output vector\&. Valid fields: yi and, only with -coeffs, coeffs\&.
.TP
-output list|vector
Output representation for every numeric result array: Tcl list or RBC vector name\&. Defaults to list; independent of -input\&.
.TP
-x values
Distinct sample positions; at least one value\&.
.TP
-xi values
Evaluation positions; must not be empty\&.
.TP
-y values
Sample values; must have the same length as -x\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Every array argument marked values uses the representation selected by -input\&. Scalar options remain
ordinary Tcl numbers\&. Numeric inputs must be finite\&. RBC support must be enabled in the build to use
vectors\&.
.PP
Vector names resolve in the caller's namespace; destination namespaces must already exist\&. Each unnamed
output, including fields omitted from -names, is created with ::rbc::vector create #auto\&. Returned
vector names are fully qualified\&.
.PP
Do not specify both -name and the yi entry of -names\&. Unknown output fields and duplicate destinations
are errors\&. The caller owns returned vectors and can release them with ::rbc::vector destroy
$vectorName\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
The interpolated values yi\&. With -coeffs, returns a dictionary with yi and coeffs arrays\&.
Each numeric array is a Tcl list by default or an RBC vector name with -output vector\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBhermiteSpline1d\fR (::tclinterp::interpolation)
.RE
.PP
Performs cubic Hermite spline interpolation\&.
.RS 4n
\fBhermiteSpline1d\fP \fI-t values -y values -yp values -ti values ?-deriv? ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-deriv
Include first derivatives in the result dictionary\&.
.TP
-ifexists error|replace
Policy for existing destination vectors; defaults to error\&. With replace, an existing real vector is resized and overwritten\&.
.TP
-input list|vector
Input representation for all array arguments: Tcl lists or real RBC vector names\&. Defaults to list\&.
.TP
-name name
Destination vector name for yi; requires -output vector\&. Omit it or use #auto to create an automatically named vector\&.
.TP
-names dictionary
Dictionary mapping output fields to destination vector names; requires -output vector\&. Valid fields: yi and, only with -deriv, yder1\&.
.TP
-output list|vector
Output representation for every numeric result array: Tcl list or RBC vector name\&. Defaults to list; independent of -input\&.
.TP
-t values
Strictly increasing sample positions; at least two values\&. Alias: -x\&.
.TP
-ti values
Evaluation positions; must not be empty\&. Alias: -xi\&.
.TP
-y values
Sample values; must have the same length as -t\&.
.TP
-yp values
First derivatives at the sample positions; same length as -t\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Every array argument marked values uses the representation selected by -input\&. Scalar options remain
ordinary Tcl numbers\&. Numeric inputs must be finite\&. RBC support must be enabled in the build to use
vectors\&.
.PP
Vector names resolve in the caller's namespace; destination namespaces must already exist\&. Each unnamed
output, including fields omitted from -names, is created with ::rbc::vector create #auto\&. Returned
vector names are fully qualified\&.
.PP
Do not specify both -name and the yi entry of -names\&. Unknown output fields and duplicate destinations
are errors\&. The caller owns returned vectors and can release them with ::rbc::vector destroy
$vectorName\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
The interpolated values yi\&. With -deriv, returns a dictionary with yi and first derivatives
yder1\&. Each numeric array is a Tcl list by default or an RBC vector name with -output vector\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBlagr1d\fR (::tclinterp::interpolation)
.RE
.PP
Performs Lagrange polynomial one-dimensional interpolation\&.
.RS 4n
\fBlagr1d\fP \fI-x values -y values -xi values ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-ifexists error|replace
Policy for existing destination vectors; defaults to error\&. With replace, an existing real vector is resized and overwritten\&.
.TP
-input list|vector
Input representation for all array arguments: Tcl lists or real RBC vector names\&. Defaults to list\&.
.TP
-name name
Destination vector name for yi; requires -output vector\&. Omit it or use #auto to create an automatically named vector\&.
.TP
-names dictionary
Dictionary mapping output fields to destination vector names; requires -output vector\&. Valid fields: yi\&.
.TP
-output list|vector
Output representation for every numeric result array: Tcl list or RBC vector name\&. Defaults to list; independent of -input\&.
.TP
-x values
Distinct sample positions; at least one value\&.
.TP
-xi values
Evaluation positions; must not be empty\&.
.TP
-y values
Sample values; must have the same length as -x\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Every array argument marked values uses the representation selected by -input\&. Scalar options remain
ordinary Tcl numbers\&. Numeric inputs must be finite\&. RBC support must be enabled in the build to use
vectors\&.
.PP
Vector names resolve in the caller's namespace; destination namespaces must already exist\&. Each unnamed
output, including fields omitted from -names, is created with ::rbc::vector create #auto\&. Returned
vector names are fully qualified\&.
.PP
Do not specify both -name and the yi entry of -names\&. Unknown output fields and duplicate destinations
are errors\&. The caller owns returned vectors and can release them with ::rbc::vector destroy
$vectorName\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
The interpolated values yi, as a Tcl list by default or an RBC vector name with -output
vector\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBleast1d\fR (::tclinterp::interpolation)
.RE
.PP
Fits a least-squares polynomial\&.
.RS 4n
\fBleast1d\fP \fI-x values -y values -xi values ?-w values? ?-nterms integer? ?-coeffs? ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-coeffs
Include polynomial coefficient arrays in the result dictionary\&.
.TP
-ifexists error|replace
Policy for existing destination vectors; defaults to error\&. With replace, an existing real vector is resized and overwritten\&.
.TP
-input list|vector
Input representation for all array arguments: Tcl lists or real RBC vector names\&. Defaults to list\&.
.TP
-name name
Destination vector name for yi; requires -output vector\&. Omit it or use #auto to create an automatically named vector\&.
.TP
-names dictionary
Dictionary mapping output fields to destination vector names; requires -output vector\&. Valid fields: yi, and, only with -coeffs, coeffs\&.b, coeffs\&.c, coeffs\&.d\&.
.TP
-nterms integer
Number of polynomial terms; defaults to 3\&. Must be positive and no greater than the number of distinct sample positions\&.
.TP
-output list|vector
Output representation for every numeric result array: Tcl list or RBC vector name\&. Defaults to list; independent of -input\&.
.TP
-w values
Optional positive weights; same length as -x\&. Defaults to all ones\&.
.TP
-x values
Sample positions; at least one value\&.
.TP
-xi values
Evaluation positions; must not be empty\&.
.TP
-y values
Sample values; must have the same length as -x\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Every array argument marked values uses the representation selected by -input\&. Scalar options remain
ordinary Tcl numbers\&. Numeric inputs must be finite\&. RBC support must be enabled in the build to use
vectors\&.
.PP
Vector names resolve in the caller's namespace; destination namespaces must already exist\&. Each unnamed
output, including fields omitted from -names, is created with ::rbc::vector create #auto\&. Returned
vector names are fully qualified\&.
.PP
Do not specify both -name and the yi entry of -names\&. Unknown output fields and duplicate destinations
are errors\&. The caller owns returned vectors and can release them with ::rbc::vector destroy
$vectorName\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
The fitted values yi, or a dictionary containing yi when -coeffs is specified\&. With
-coeffs, the dictionary also contains coeffs, a nested dictionary with keys b, c, and d\&. Each
numeric array is a Tcl list by default or an RBC vector name with -output vector\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBleast1dDer\fR (::tclinterp::interpolation)
.RE
.PP
Fits a least-squares polynomial and evaluates its first derivative\&.
.RS 4n
\fBleast1dDer\fP \fI-x values -y values -xi values ?-w values? ?-nterms integer? ?-coeffs? ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-coeffs
Include polynomial coefficient arrays in the result dictionary\&.
.TP
-ifexists error|replace
Policy for existing destination vectors; defaults to error\&. With replace, an existing real vector is resized and overwritten\&.
.TP
-input list|vector
Input representation for all array arguments: Tcl lists or real RBC vector names\&. Defaults to list\&.
.TP
-name name
Destination vector name for yi; requires -output vector\&. Omit it or use #auto to create an automatically named vector\&.
.TP
-names dictionary
Dictionary mapping output fields to destination vector names; requires -output vector\&. Valid fields: yi, yiDer, and, only with -coeffs, coeffs\&.b, coeffs\&.c, coeffs\&.d\&.
.TP
-nterms integer
Number of polynomial terms; defaults to 3\&. Must be positive and no greater than the number of distinct sample positions\&.
.TP
-output list|vector
Output representation for every numeric result array: Tcl list or RBC vector name\&. Defaults to list; independent of -input\&.
.TP
-w values
Optional positive weights; same length as -x\&. Defaults to all ones\&.
.TP
-x values
Sample positions; at least one value\&.
.TP
-xi values
Evaluation positions; must not be empty\&.
.TP
-y values
Sample values; must have the same length as -x\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Every array argument marked values uses the representation selected by -input\&. Scalar options remain
ordinary Tcl numbers\&. Numeric inputs must be finite\&. RBC support must be enabled in the build to use
vectors\&.
.PP
Vector names resolve in the caller's namespace; destination namespaces must already exist\&. Each unnamed
output, including fields omitted from -names, is created with ::rbc::vector create #auto\&. Returned
vector names are fully qualified\&.
.PP
Do not specify both -name and the yi entry of -names\&. Unknown output fields and duplicate destinations
are errors\&. The caller owns returned vectors and can release them with ::rbc::vector destroy
$vectorName\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
A dictionary with yi values and yiDer first derivatives\&. With -coeffs, the dictionary also
contains coeffs, a nested dictionary with keys b, c, and d\&. Each numeric array is a Tcl list by
default or an RBC vector name with -output vector\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBlin1d\fR (::tclinterp::interpolation)
.RE
.PP
Performs linear one-dimensional interpolation\&.
.RS 4n
\fBlin1d\fP \fI-x values -y values -xi values ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-ifexists error|replace
Policy for existing destination vectors; defaults to error\&. With replace, an existing real vector is resized and overwritten\&.
.TP
-input list|vector
Input representation for all array arguments: Tcl lists or real RBC vector names\&. Defaults to list\&.
.TP
-name name
Destination vector name for yi; requires -output vector\&. Omit it or use #auto to create an automatically named vector\&.
.TP
-names dictionary
Dictionary mapping output fields to destination vector names; requires -output vector\&. Valid fields: yi\&.
.TP
-output list|vector
Output representation for every numeric result array: Tcl list or RBC vector name\&. Defaults to list; independent of -input\&.
.TP
-x values
Strictly increasing sample positions; at least two values\&.
.TP
-xi values
Evaluation positions; must not be empty\&.
.TP
-y values
Sample values; must have the same length as -x\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Every array argument marked values uses the representation selected by -input\&. Scalar options remain
ordinary Tcl numbers\&. Numeric inputs must be finite\&. RBC support must be enabled in the build to use
vectors\&.
.PP
Vector names resolve in the caller's namespace; destination namespaces must already exist\&. Each unnamed
output, including fields omitted from -names, is created with ::rbc::vector create #auto\&. Returned
vector names are fully qualified\&.
.PP
Do not specify both -name and the yi entry of -names\&. Unknown output fields and duplicate destinations
are errors\&. The caller owns returned vectors and can release them with ::rbc::vector destroy
$vectorName\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
The interpolated values yi, as a Tcl list by default or an RBC vector name with -output
vector\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBnear1d\fR (::tclinterp::interpolation)
.RE
.PP
Performs nearest-neighbor one-dimensional interpolation\&.
.RS 4n
\fBnear1d\fP \fI-x values -y values -xi values ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-ifexists error|replace
Policy for existing destination vectors; defaults to error\&. With replace, an existing real vector is resized and overwritten\&.
.TP
-input list|vector
Input representation for all array arguments: Tcl lists or real RBC vector names\&. Defaults to list\&.
.TP
-name name
Destination vector name for yi; requires -output vector\&. Omit it or use #auto to create an automatically named vector\&.
.TP
-names dictionary
Dictionary mapping output fields to destination vector names; requires -output vector\&. Valid fields: yi\&.
.TP
-output list|vector
Output representation for every numeric result array: Tcl list or RBC vector name\&. Defaults to list; independent of -input\&.
.TP
-x values
Sample positions; at least one value\&.
.TP
-xi values
Evaluation positions; must not be empty\&.
.TP
-y values
Sample values; must have the same length as -x\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Every array argument marked values uses the representation selected by -input\&. Scalar options remain
ordinary Tcl numbers\&. Numeric inputs must be finite\&. RBC support must be enabled in the build to use
vectors\&.
.PP
Vector names resolve in the caller's namespace; destination namespaces must already exist\&. Each unnamed
output, including fields omitted from -names, is created with ::rbc::vector create #auto\&. Returned
vector names are fully qualified\&.
.PP
Do not specify both -name and the yi entry of -names\&. Unknown output fields and duplicate destinations
are errors\&. The caller owns returned vectors and can release them with ::rbc::vector destroy
$vectorName\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
The interpolated values yi, as a Tcl list by default or an RBC vector name with -output
vector\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBpchip1d\fR (::tclinterp::interpolation)
.RE
.PP
Performs piecewise cubic Hermite interpolation (PCHIP)\&.
.RS 4n
\fBpchip1d\fP \fI-x values -f values -xe values ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-f values
Sample values; same length as -x\&. Alias: -y\&.
.TP
-ifexists error|replace
Policy for existing destination vectors; defaults to error\&. With replace, an existing real vector is resized and overwritten\&.
.TP
-input list|vector
Input representation for all array arguments: Tcl lists or real RBC vector names\&. Defaults to list\&.
.TP
-name name
Destination vector name for yi; requires -output vector\&. Omit it or use #auto to create an automatically named vector\&.
.TP
-names dictionary
Dictionary mapping output fields to destination vector names; requires -output vector\&. Valid fields: yi\&.
.TP
-output list|vector
Output representation for every numeric result array: Tcl list or RBC vector name\&. Defaults to list; independent of -input\&.
.TP
-x values
Strictly increasing sample positions; at least two values\&.
.TP
-xe values
Evaluation positions; must not be empty\&. Alias: -xi\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Every array argument marked values uses the representation selected by -input\&. Scalar options remain
ordinary Tcl numbers\&. Numeric inputs must be finite\&. RBC support must be enabled in the build to use
vectors\&.
.PP
Vector names resolve in the caller's namespace; destination namespaces must already exist\&. Each unnamed
output, including fields omitted from -names, is created with ::rbc::vector create #auto\&. Returned
vector names are fully qualified\&.
.PP
Do not specify both -name and the yi entry of -names\&. Unknown output fields and duplicate destinations
are errors\&. The caller owns returned vectors and can release them with ::rbc::vector destroy
$vectorName\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
The interpolated values yi, as a Tcl list by default or an RBC vector name with -output
vector\&.


